{
  "area": "martinique",
  "method": "Martinique, whole island: the Anses d'Arlet and Diamant coast (south), Trois-Îlets, and the north Caribbean coast from Schoelcher through Saint-Pierre to Le Prêcheur. No official marine-park or government dive-site or mooring list exists online (the DEAL Martinique geology fiche on the Rocher du Diamant is not a site list), so the Martinique tourism site (martinique-tour.com, the tourism directory that also carries the club profiles of A Papa D'Lo Saint-Pierre and Diamant Sub Club) stands in as one list. Operator lists read in French: O Fil de l'Eau (Grande Anse d'Arlet, 27-site map and exploration pages), Espace Plongée Martinique (Pointe du Bout, its sites section), Canopée Bleue (Anses d'Arlet), Corail Club Caraïbes (Anse à l'Âne) and Alpha Plongée (Grande Anse). A Papa D'Lo and Diamant Sub Club have no site list of their own online (dead or parked domains), so their sites rest on the tourism profiles only. A site is counted when named on at least two independent lists; sites on one list stay as excluded. Name merges: Anse Dufour is also Pointe Dufour; Anse 3 Airs is also Anse 3 Aires; the Tombant des Anses is also the Tombant d'Arlet; Petites and Grandes Jorasses are one row because three operators publish them together, and only the Petites Jorasses (0-25 m) are inside recreational depth. The Roraima (50-60 m) is technical depth and excluded. The Saint-Pierre wrecks other than the Roraima, the northern cayes, and Diamant-area sites (Caye d'Obian, L'Arche, Fer à Cheval) are each on one list only, so they are excluded; the Saint-Pierre side is therefore thin because no Saint-Pierre or Diamant operator publishes a site list. Counted 2026-10-14.",
